  "body": "File this issue per request in [Bug 591737 comment 234](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=591737#c234).  \n\nThe question was the z-ordering of two absolutely positioned elements, where one is a child of the <summary> and one is a child of the <details> that comes before <summary> in the DOM (assuming neither <summary> nor <details> are absolute containing blocks)\n\nThe test case is here. https://jsfiddle.net/aethanyc/mk2fd\n\nCurrently, both Chrome and Firefox implementation in progress in [Bug 591737](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=591737) put the absolute div in <summary> in the back. It might be good to note the z-order of the children in <summary>.\n",
